nd kind (fact 9).\n2. Fact 11 states that all blue, kind things are rough. Therefore, Harry must be rough.\n3. Fact 12 states that rough, kind things are quiet. If Harry were rough, he would have to be quiet.\n4. However, Harry is not quiet because he's blue (fact 18: if something is quiet and not blue, it's young; but Harry is blue, so he can't be quiet).\n5. Therefore, Harry cannot be rough because that would require him to be quiet, which contradicts his blue status.\n6. Hence, the statement \"Harry is rough\" is false.\n\n**Answer:** B) False",
