messages:   10%|#         | 62/600 [54:02<10:00:24, 66.96s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is blue. Anne is rough. Bob is cold. Bob is green. Bob is rough. Bob is white. Dave is blue. Dave is white. Harry is young. If Bob is big then Bob is white. Young people are white. Cold, young people are rough. If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white. White, big people are blue. All blue people are green. If someone is young and white then they are big. Blue people are cold.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Harry is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me start by breaking down all the information provided and see how it connects.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the facts given:\n\n1.Anne is big.\n2.Anne is blue.\n3.Anne is rough.\n4.Bob is cold.\n5.Bob is green.\n6.Bob is rough.\n7.Bob is white.\n8.Dave is blue.\n9.Dave is white.\n10.Harry is young.\n11.If Bob is big then Bob is white.\n12.Young people are white.\n13.Cold, young people are rough.\n14.If Anne is green and Anne is young then Anne is white.\n15.White, big people are blue.\n16.All blue people are green.\n17.If someone is young and white then they are big.\n18.Blue people are cold.\n\nNow, the question is about Harry.From point 10, we know Harry is young.Let\'s see what else we can deduce about Harry.\n\nFrom point 12: Young people are white.Since Harry is young, he must be white.So Harry is white.\n\nNow, looking at point 17: If someone is young and white, then they are big.Harry is both young and white, so according to this rule, Harry must be big.So that would make the statement "Harry is big" true.\n\nWait, but let me double-check to make sure I\'m not missing anything.Let\'s go through each relevant point again.\n\nHarry is young (10).Young people are white (12), so Harry is white.Then, since Harry is young and white, per point 17, he must be big.So yes, Harry is big.\nThere is no conflicting information to consider when determining whether Harry is big.</think>.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
