 red (point 14). But Harry is not red; Dave is red. So Harry can't be cold because that would make him red, which contradicts the given information.\n\nTherefore, Harry is not cold. So the statement \"Harry is cold\" is false.\n\nWait, but let me check again. Harry is big, so he's young. If he were cold, he'd be red. But he's not red, so he can't be cold. So the answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nHarry is not cold because if he were, he would be red, but he isn't. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
